{
    "name": "Rastreador Brasileiro",
    "alt_name": "Urrador Americano",
    "description": "The Rastreador Brasileiro is a mid- to large-sized breed of dog—specifically a scent hound—from Brazil. in 1967, by 1973, an outbreak of disease and an overdose of insecticides, effectively eliminated the breed's entire population. However, efforts were made to reproduce the Rastreador Brasileiro through mixing and controlled breeding projects involving several other hound breeds, resulting in today's Rastreador Brasileiro.",
